load_theory — retained server obligations
==================================================

Status: retained contract; current carve-out verification pending.

Load a theory and its dependencies through Headless.Session.use_theories. Resolve session-qualified names through the session structure or use master_dir. Return per-theory status and positioned messages. Preserve cancellation and document-mutation serialization. No resource registration or source attachment follows loading. Also the sole re-check path: use_theories re-reads the file fresh on every call, so calling load_theory again after an on-disk edit is already "check_theory" -- there is no separate tool or method for it (retired 2026-09-12, see CHANGELOG and spec D-2026-09-12-retire-check-theory).

Verification obligations
------------------------

T1 [bridge] A well-formed theory under master_dir loads successfully.

T2 [bridge] A broken theory reports an error with positioned messages.

T3 [bridge] Session-qualified names resolve without master_dir through the startup session structure.

T4 [bridge] Loading an unchanged theory succeeds.

T6 [e2e] Load a filesystem fixture, edit it, and check the edited file through the retained public tools.

T7 [bridge] Load a valid fixture, edit it to introduce an error, load again and observe that error, then fix and load again successfully. (migrated from the retired check_theory#T1: load_theory re-reads the file fresh on every call, so re-checking after an edit is the same call, not a separate tool.)

T8 [bridge] Loading a never-loaded filesystem theory succeeds when the source is valid. (migrated from check_theory#T2.)

T9 [bridge] Warnings remain diagnostics without becoming fatal errors; errors make loading fail. (migrated from check_theory#T3.)

T10 [e2e] The public tool workflow loads, edits and re-loads a theory and reports the changed source accurately. (migrated from check_theory#T4.)
